279	 * The fields a record's parameters are checked against.
280	 *
281	 * A schema with variants is chosen by the record's own discriminator when it has one (a caller's
282	 * kind, or a code operation the record carries). When the record does not carry the discriminator,
283	 * the parameters must satisfy at least one variant: the effect a variant names is the effect the
284	 * parameters describe, so the record is valid when they describe one of them.
